From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: Vertex outputs for tessellation are not packed by component

Outputs sharing a location (Component decorations) were packed into one m_location_N vector when the
vertex shader captures them to a buffer, also for tessellation, where that buffer is the tessellation
control shader's input. The tessellation control shader does not pack its inputs (component packing in
tessellation shaders is not supported, 'HACK 20542' lets the decorations through): it reads one member
per variable, ordered by location and component. The two layouts disagreed: dxil-spirv's POSITION (float3,
location 0) and TEXCOORD (float, location 0 component 3) of Ratchet & Clank: Rift Apart's tessellation
pipelines (steamac #49) were written as 'float4 m_location_0' (16 bytes a vertex) and read as
'float3 POSITION; float TEXCOORD;' (32 bytes), so control points came from the wrong vertices and nothing
was drawn. Vertex outputs for tessellation are declared like the control shader's inputs now.
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index dcaf1866..1511e6b4 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -5702,10 +5702,13 @@ uint32_t CompilerMSL::add_interface_block(StorageClass storage, bool patch, bool
 	// Varying interfaces between stages which use "user()" attribute can be dealt with
 	// without explicit packing and unpacking of components. For any variables which link against the runtime
 	// in some way (vertex attributes, fragment output, etc), we'll need to deal with it somehow.
+	// The outputs of a vertex shader for tessellation are read by the tessellation control shader, whose inputs
+	// are not packed (one member per variable, ordered by location and component): pack neither side.
 	bool pack_components =
 	    (storage == StorageClassInput && get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelVertex) ||
 	    (storage == StorageClassOutput && get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelFragment) ||
-	    (storage == StorageClassOutput && get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelVertex && capture_output_to_buffer);
+	    (storage == StorageClassOutput && get_execution_model() == ExecutionModelVertex && capture_output_to_buffer &&
+	     !msl_options.vertex_for_tessellation);
 
 	ir.for_each_typed_id<SPIRVariable>([&](uint32_t var_id, SPIRVariable &var) {
 		if (var.storage != storage)
